# Produced by stdlib/asterui/tests/font_adapter_test.ast under
# qemu-aarch64 (run twice, stdout byte-identical, exit 0).
# RTADV: hmtx advances in native px at scale 1 (48 px em).
# GLYPHHASH <name> <cp> <src> <hash>: FNV-1a 64-bit over the staged
# 8bpp coverage bitmap (48 rows TT, taller for descender glyphs:
# g 55, p 54, y 54, j 54, q 54 rows; 48x48 CJK fallback, 24x24 ASCII
# fallback), printed as signed decimal. src 1 = system font,
# 2 = hand-drawn ASCII, 3 = hand-drawn CJK atlas. Bitmaps are
# rasterized from face 2 (SC) of
# /usr/share/fonts/opentype/noto/NotoSansCJK-Regular.ttc (CFF
# outlines) for src 1; src 2/3 are OUR OWN hand-drawn bitmaps
# (zero third-party font IP). RTFB: fallback events, last reason
# (1 = no file), missing-glyph count.
# SCAN <sc> <rows> <err...>: the discovery scan enumerates all
# seven candidate names (no early return); errs are 1 = missing,
# 0 = loaded. Section G (v2.1 blob fix, 2026-11-14) freezes the
# corrected bowl glyphs (e/o/a/g/c/p/0/5/6, U+5DF2), the flex
# glyphs (flex1 U+8C99 Regular, flex1_bold U+5D67 Bold, hflex
# U+585B), and the font-switch check (A_bold differs from A, A3
# equals A). The pre-existing hashes (zhong/wen/zeng/han/A) are
# unchanged by that fix: ops 26/27/30/31 keep byte-identical
# behaviour for 4/5-arg uses. Section H (v2.3 descender fix,
# 2026-11-14) changes exactly two G hashes for the documented
# reason -- g 169677861573791286 -> 6861362426131676361 and p
# 1182715790780022136 -> -6050333832807142197, because their
# bitmaps grew from 48 to 55 / 54 rows to hold the descender ink
# that the old fixed cell clipped -- and adds y/j/q/g_bold.
# Section I (v2.4 CFF2 default instance, 2026-11-14) adds the
# _cff2 hashes (the CFF2 subset fixture renders byte-identical
# to the CFF Regular hashes of sections C/G -- same outlines,
# same upm -- so each _cff2 hash EQUALS its CFF twin) and the
# _blend hashes (A_blend == B_blend proves blend at the default
# instance keeps the defaults and drops the deltas; C/D render
# with ink). RTFB moves 1 1 1 -> 2 6 1 for a documented reason:
# the truncated CFF2 fixture is a second fallback event
# (reason 6 = CFF2 present but unparsable). No pre-existing
# hash moves in this round.
# Every other hash is unchanged by that fix, including all CJK
# hashes (CJK ink stays above the old cell bottom) and e/o/a/c/
# 0/5/6/yi3/flex1/hflex. Hashes change if the TrueType
# parser/rasterizer, the face selection, the hmtx advance scan,
# the vertical mapping, or the fallback upscaler changes -- that
# is expected; regenerate deliberately and say why. The old .auf
# baselines are void: no .auf file exists in this repo, so no
# .auf-era hash can recur.
# v2.5 (2026-11-14): section J (custom fonts) adds 83 lines --
# 4 weight 'A' hashes (Light/Regular/Medium/Bold, all different)
# + 4 RTADV hyzy_weight lines (300/400/500/700) + 14 Regular
# probe hashes with INK lines + 46 hyzy_spec hashes (every
# distinct specimen glyph) + A_hyzy_again. The ONLY old line that
# moves is RTFB: "2 6 1" -> "2 5 1", because the broken CFF2
# fixture (cff2_broken.ttf, CFF2 table extent 612..763 overruns
# its 686-byte file) is now caught by the parse_sfnt table
# validation and fails with err 5 (no usable outline table)
# instead of err 6 (CFF2 present but unparsable); err 6 is
# reserved for a CFF2 table that is fully present but fails to
# parse. Section J's missing/corrupt loads add no fallback
# event (the system face is restored), so the event count stays 2.
# Engine ink (INK lines) is cross-checked against FreeType 48px
# no-hinting offline: most glyphs within 5%, thin/dense glyphs
# up to -20% (Medium 'j') -- the pre-existing scanline-sampler
# limit (thin AA fringes are dropped), not an outline error;
# shapes are verified by ASCII art (see fontcustom/compare.out).
